{
  "dom_id": "step-e10749",
  "name": "Example: Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid",
  "problem": "Which of the diagrams below shows three collinear points?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/c0df27c96da9f9c285438faee93652f81362fe91a51dc28e02ec0e2e9ff42177.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/4967d8325f8ed8415a8404286d29ff97eb65cd6926ed1ca27a943178aee1a3cc.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/af746af6fba54f69570f5dcfa38fbbb4cffd290080cc45deec433bc5266aa75e.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/c0d9d178c5be09aa7f6ad1927c6f8e930154cf077aabbd18a765820babd63069.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e10749\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e10749\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <p>Which of the diagrams below shows three collinear points?</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-901df5646c3c7ac7b2bccfd60816ae22\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/901df5646c3c7ac7b2bccfd60816ae22\"></div>\n                    </div>     \n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                        <p>Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram I shows three points that are <em>not</em> collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-5442fcd818eeb76bfbde3515a8cd2367\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/5442fcd818eeb76bfbde3515a8cd2367\"></div>\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-6062c638039bd28cbfbb5a1ea3936397\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/6062c638039bd28cbfbb5a1ea3936397\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram III shows three points that are <em>not</em> collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-4486a38d04b631a72e14f1dabebaaee6\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/4486a38d04b631a72e14f1dabebaaee6\"></div>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"</p>\n\n                    </div>     \n                </div>                            \n                    \n            </div>",
